From ef4de72a05de4b4dee90b1ed5731517ce2c3bb74 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 00:59:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] The Table review (U17): next devotion opens at its top,
 one event a night, steadier wake lock

- Before this / Next on a devotion page kept the page mounted and left the
  reader at the bottom of the next devotion; it now starts at the top.
- "We did this tonight" sends family_devotion_complete once per devotion per
  night on this device, however many taps (recordDevotionDone reports
  `already`).
- The wake lock is asked again on the next tap or key when the browser
  refused the first ask (it is made after a fetch, away from the tap), and is
  dropped from memory when the browser lets it go.
- /family/devotions?tab=<set>&day=N opens that day's own page, so U13's
  Advent links land on the devotion rather than the list.
- The season list on /family comes from the static year map without waiting
  for the index; the tonight card is labelled by its always-present eyebrow.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
